<Text>&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt&quot;&gt;OFDM-based Wideband Hybrid Beamforming Systems&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;H2 class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;This example demonstrates a complete link-level OFDM-based wideband hybrid beamforming system: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;it&amp;nbsp;comprises of complete source, channel and receiver.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Supported Features:&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 1. Support flexible beamforming structure, including full digital beamforming, hybrid beamforming and full RF/analog beamforming.&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2. For hybrid beamforming and full RF/analog beamforming, a reference algorithm model is provided to train wideband OFDM-based RF beamforming in transmitter and receiver given estimated channel status&amp;nbsp;independent of digital beamforming process (i.e. MIMO precoding), where the&amp;nbsp;training solution is based on a pre-defined training process.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;3. OFDM MIMO source and receiver can be configured to&amp;nbsp;wideband signal with different frame structure. In typical settings, there are two preambles, the first preamble is used for the synchronization in the receiver, and the second preamble is used to train transmitter RF beamforming and receiver RF beamforming in the receiver.&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;4. In OFDM MIMO, digital beamforming process (MIMO precoding) can be turned on or off.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;5. A 3D MIMO channel is provided supporting user-defined scenario per 3GPP 3D MIMO standard and NYU scenario for mmWave frequency.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;6. Support custom antenna element pattern import and RF impairment, when custom antenna element pattern is imported, parameters BearingAngle, DowntiltAngle and SlantAngle can be set accordingly to rotate the antenna element pattern to appropriate coordinate system.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;7. Support transmitter and receiver 3D beam plotting&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;8. Support BER measurement and received constellation plotting&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Settings Notes:&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;Flexible configurations are supported by the hybrid beamforming architecture.&lt;BR&gt;In the following, parameters configuration with respect to 3 types of beamforming architectures and the common parameters are listed.&lt;BR&gt;For easy comparison to ideal QPSK, current example configures the architecture to RF/analog beamforming and simulation with Omni antenna element pattern.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;The configuration for&amp;nbsp;aforementioned three beamforming modes are&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;Digital beamforming&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp; RF channels = 16 (from the output of FlexOFDM MIMO)&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; TxAntennaArrayMask and RxAntennaArrayMask should be set to&amp;nbsp;identity diagonal matrix&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; The algorithm model to train RF beamforming is not used&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; Digital beamforming process (MIMO precoding) can be enabled, and the precoding gain can be observed from the simulation.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;RF/analog beamforming&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp; RF channels = 1 (from the output of FlexOFDM MIMO)&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; The algorithm model to train RF beamforming is used to get RF beaforming in both transmitter and receiver.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; Digital beamforming process (MIMO precoding) is not used&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Hybrid beamforming&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp; RF channels = 2, 4, or 8 (from the output of FlexOFDM MIMO)&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; The algorithm model to train RF beamforming is used to get RF beaforming in both transmitter and receiver.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; Digital beamforming process (MIMO precoding) can be enabled, and the precoding gain can be observed from the simulation.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Common parameters:&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp; FFT Size = 64, Bandwidth = 2G, Central Frequency = 28.5GHz&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; Transmit antennas = 16, receiver antennas = 4&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; MIMO channel is set to NYU use-defined with one or two predefined AOA and AOD.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; One OFDM symbol for Preamble 1 for synchronization&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; Multiple OFDM symbols for Preamble 2 for RF beamforming training (defined in equation based on other parameters)&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp; In data part, one pilot is allocated per every three subcarriers for channel estimation. The total number of data symbols is configurable.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Regarding RF beamforming&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;For RF/analog beamforming and hybrid beamforming, RF beamforming in both transmitter and receiver is the key advantage to improve signal quality (SNR). There is one reference algorithm model in this workspace to calculate optimal RF beamforming in both transmitter and receiver with the assistance of preamble data. Ideally, the maximum total SNR gain (in dB) of RF beamforming is 10*log10(Nt)+10*log10(Nr), where Nt is the number of transmitter antennas and Nr is the number of receiver antennas.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Other Configuration Notice&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;All&amp;nbsp;configurations are collected in &quot;Equations&quot;&amp;nbsp;Tab of the schematic&amp;nbsp;and relavant comments are attached following the corresponding settings and s&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;ampling rate.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;1.&amp;nbsp;The number of antenna elements in x&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;-axis direction should equals to one when UPA/ULA is applied.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;2.&amp;nbsp;the way to construct the vectors, such as TxPosition_X, TxPosition_Y, TxPosition_Z, TxAntennaArrayMask, TxPhaseShifterDistortion in Tx.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;As for TxPosition_X, TxPosition_Y and&amp;nbsp;TxPosition_Z, the order of the elements in these vectors&amp;nbsp;are antenna in y-axis first, in z-axis second and in x-axis third. The length of these vectors is Nt. The &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;structure of counterparts &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;in &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Rx is similar.&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;As for TxAntennaArrayMask, the dimension is Nt-by-Ntrf. The first&amp;nbsp;column correspond to the connections between the first RF chain and each antenna &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;elements, and the second &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;column &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;corresponds to the connnections between the second RF chain and each antenna elements, and so on. The value of each element is 0 or 1. 1 indicates connected and 0 indicates disabled. &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The structure of &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;counterparts in Rx is the same.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;As for TxPhaseShifterDistortion, the dimension is also Nt-by-Ntrf. The structure is the same as TxAntennaArrayMask. But the value of each element can be complex which &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;represents the &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;amplitude distortion and phase distortion.&lt;BR&gt;Where, Ntrf and Nrrf&amp;nbsp;are the numbers of RF chains in Tx and Rx side, respectively.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;3. Dynamic 3D plot show the beams of each tx stream and rx stream&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;. Combined beam of all tx antennas is also shown in the figure.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;5. T&lt;/SPAN&gt;he angle scopes for plotting are [0,180] for zenith and 0,360] for azimuth, so the mirror radiation pattern would show in case of ULA and UPA configuration. The plotting granularity is 1&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;degree.&lt;BR&gt;6. Configure the channel model accordingly if the number of streams are changed.&lt;BR&gt;7. If Digital Beamforming is applied, set TxAntennaArrayMask&amp;nbsp;= eye(Nt) and RxAntennaArrayMask = eye(Nr),&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;but please keep parameters&amp;nbsp;TxAntennaArrayMask in RF_Tx_WB and RxAntennaArrayMask in RF_Rx_WB as ones(Nt,Ntrf) and ones(Nr,Nrrf) respectively, since these two subnets are common for Preamble 1 part, Preamble 2 part and Data part. The real TxAntennaArrayMask and RxAntennaArrayMask can be set to other modules and it will work accordingly.&lt;BR&gt;8. If multi-path channel is introduced, the parameter TMax should be set longer than&amp;nbsp;the multi-path delay to get a correct channel estimation.&lt;BR&gt;9.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt; Usually, antenna engineers output antenna element radiation pattern file with the maximum power pointing to zenith, which conflicts with the antenna array placement in Y-Z plane, so please change DowntileAngle of each antenna element to -90 and remain BearingAngle and SlantAngle unchanged.&lt;BR&gt;10. SubtractionDuetoCH = 0.306dB (16Tx4Rx) and SubtractionDuetoCH = 0.345dB (64Tx16Rx, 64Tx8Rx)&amp;nbsp;need subtracted from the signal&apos;s simulation SNR due to the power boost introduced by 3D channel model. Please note that the value is only available in current configuration and it should be adjusted according to the channel configuration (including parameter &quot;Seed&quot; and the number of antennas).&lt;BR&gt;11. Parameter &lt;STRONG&gt;SNR&lt;/STRONG&gt; in &quot;Interpolation Setting category&quot; in RxAlgorithm tab of module FelxOFDM_Receiver_RF should equal to the simulation SNR.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Notes about Configurations&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;1. If more antenna elements number is needed, please increase the number of RF chains accordingly to avoid endless simulation. Based on the design, Preamble2 will transmit (Nt/Ntrf)*(Nr/Nrrf) OFDM-type training symbols. Upon current number of RF chains (Ntrf=Nrrf=1), Preamble2 will transmit Nt*Nr OFDM-type training symbols. To be specific,&amp;nbsp;if 64Tx64Rx,&amp;nbsp;128Tx64Rx&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;256Tx64Rx means Preamble2 contains 4096, 8192 and 16384 OFDM-type symbols, respectively, which will be&amp;nbsp;heavily time-consuming&amp;nbsp;configurations and they are not reasonable configurations in reality as well.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;</Text>
